{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/543706-how-to-map-out-a-tangled-web-of-alliances-and-rivalries","id":543706,"title":"How to map out a tangled web of alliances and rivalries?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-07T04:00:10-07:00","id":543706,"title":"How to map out a tangled web of alliances and rivalries?","content":"So I was thinking of doing an rpg based on the setting of the old Dos game Master of Orion II. A lot of the details of the setting, the various alien races and their cultures is basically left up to the player to imagine, and just for kicks I thought I would take what information there is and expand on it and make it into a RPG setting of my own.<br /> <br /> So I found a website that lists the various races and how the different races are predisposed to one another. (I don't know that I have ever noticed this in the game, but that's not really important for my purposes.)<br /> <br /> The problem is figuring out a way to map this all out so I can visualize it. I can map out the alliances pretty easy, or the rivalries, but finding a way to map both out simultaneously without it turning into a jumbled mess is proving difficult.<br /> <br /> I know some WOD games make use of such maps, but there are usually no more than 5 or 6 factions on the page. I would like to plot 13 different factions. 0_0<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any tools they might suggest, or techniques? Programs? Websites?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T09:26:58-07:00","id":545397,"title":"","content":"There might be something viable in something like roll20 or storium or the like, apart from that the only thing I can think of is doing a search for multi-layer relationship diagram tools of the sort you use in software design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:39:43-07:00","id":545891,"title":"","content":"Visio might work. But it is expensive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}